{"seq":14,"slug":"shader-programming","title":"着色器编程","stage":"DONE","category":"game-development","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"着色器编程\">着色器编程</h1><p>显卡上每秒钟有数十亿次微小的程序在并行运行：它们决定每个顶点落在屏幕的哪个位置，决定每个像素最终是什么颜色。这些跑在 GPU 上的小程序就是着色器（shader）。学会写它们，意味着你不再受限于引擎给定的材质球，而是能亲手定义光怎么照、表面怎么反射、画面如何被一层层加工——从一片草地的风吹效果到整屏的辉光与色调映射，背后都是着色器在工作。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 把着色器编程拆成四条层层递进的主线，每一章都建立在前一章的基础之上。</p>\n<p>第一条线是「基础」。要写着色器，先得知道数据如何在 GPU 里流动：顶点经过哪些可编程阶段、光栅化在哪一步发生、片元着色器拿到的插值数据从何而来。同时你需要掌握书写着色器的语言（HLSL 与 GLSL），以及贯穿一切计算的坐标空间与矩阵变换。这一章解决「着色器到底在算什么、在哪算」的问题。</p>\n<p>第二条线是「着色技法」。有了管线和语言，就可以回答最核心的问题：一个表面为什么看起来是它现在的样子。这一章讲光照模型与 BRDF（从经验性的 Phong 到物理可信的微表面理论），讲纹理如何被采样和过滤，最后落到当下工业界的事实标准——基于物理的渲染（PBR）材质。这是从「能画出东西」到「画得可信」的跨越。</p>\n<p>第三条线是「高级效果」。当单个物体的着色已经掌握，视野就扩展到整帧画面与通用计算。后处理把渲染结果当作一张图再加工，计算着色器让 GPU 跳出图形管线做并行计算，程序化噪声则用数学函数凭空生成无穷无尽的纹理与地形。这一章是着色器从「描述表面」走向「创造内容与改造画面」的地方。</p>\n<p>第四条线是「优化与工具」。再漂亮的效果，跑不到目标帧率就没有意义。这一章讲如何度量与优化着色器性能（占用率、带宽、分支），如何用 RenderDoc 等工具调试看不见的 GPU 状态，以及如何让同一份着色器跨 Direct3D、Vulkan、Metal、WebGPU 等平台编译运行。它把前三章的知识带回工程现实。</p>\n<p>四章读下来，你会从「GPU 在做什么」一路走到「如何写出可信、可扩展且高性能的着色器」。建议按顺序阅读：后面的每一章都默认你已经熟悉前面的概念，文中遇到已讲过的主题会以交叉链接指回它的主篇，而不再重复展开。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"gpu-pipeline","title":"GPU 渲染管线","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/foundations/gpu-pipeline"},{"seq":2,"slug":"shader-languages","title":"着色器语言 HLSL/GLSL","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/foundations/shader-languages"},{"seq":3,"slug":"coordinate-spaces","title":"坐标空间与变换","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/foundations/coordinate-spaces"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"shading-techniques","title":"着色技法","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/shading-techniques","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"lighting-models","title":"光照模型与 BRDF","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/shading-techniques/lighting-models"},{"seq":2,"slug":"texturing-sampling","title":"纹理与采样","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/shading-techniques/texturing-sampling"},{"seq":3,"slug":"pbr-materials","title":"PBR 材质","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/shading-techniques/pbr-materials"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"advanced-effects","title":"高级效果","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/advanced-effects","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"post-processing","title":"后处理效果","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/advanced-effects/post-processing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"compute-shaders","title":"计算着色器","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/advanced-effects/compute-shaders"},{"seq":3,"slug":"procedural-noise","title":"程序化纹理与噪声","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/advanced-effects/procedural-noise"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"optimization-tools","title":"优化与工具","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/optimization-tools","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"shader-optimization","title":"着色器性能优化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/optimization-tools/shader-optimization"},{"seq":2,"slug":"shader-debugging","title":"调试与剖析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/optimization-tools/shader-debugging"},{"seq":3,"slug":"cross-platform-shaders","title":"跨平台与着色器编译","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/shader-programming/optimization-tools/cross-platform-shaders"}]}]}